      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3.1 State Government Structure"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Chhattisgarh's governance structure comprises the State Executive, Legislature, and Judiciary.",
        "The administrative setup is categorized into 5 major divisions: Raipur, Bilaspur, Bastar, Surguja, and Durg.",
        "The state follows a 3-tier Panchayati Raj System for rural local self-governance.",
        "State Police Structure is hierarchically organized under the Director General of Police (DGP) and includes specialized forces for state security.",
        "Constitutional provisions specifically address tribal governance, special administrative rights, and executive powers of the Governor and Chief Minister."
      ],
      "id": "4c8x8el"
